   "key": "§ Architecture decision records > 001 — Sensitive storage falls back, then repairs",
   "hash": "083cc017046b6ffd",
   "does": "Claims: when EncryptionManager is unavailable (before first unlock), archive writes plaintext with .completeFileProtection, records the session in PendingEncryptionLedger, and reencryptPendingSessions() rewrites it encrypted at the next launch where the key is reachable; the window is 'bounded by one app launch'; only a throwing encrypt() is logged at .error, while the key-unavailable fallback is not logged and shows only as the ledger entry. Verified the write options (Archive+PendingEncryption.swift:18-30), encryptOrReportFailure (Archive+SessionCodec.swift:113-126: isAvailable guard returns nil silently, catch logs .error), and the launch-time repair called from ArchiveMigrations.runDeferredMigrations.",
   "entry": null,
